   "RaceName": "State Representative Pos. 2",
   "Statement": "<b>Elected Experience</b><br><br><span>Representative for the 2nd Legislative District, former Eatonville School Director, former Vice-Chair 2nd LD Pierce County Republicans, and elected PCO.</span><br><br><b>Other Professional Experience</b><br><br><span>Small business owner; </span><em><span>honorably discharged</span></em><span> Army Captain and </span><em><span>combat veteran</span></em><span> with 16 years of service (two overseas tours); 24 years in the medical field (14 as a physician assistant); 12 years as an adjunct professor at the University of Maryland.</span><br><br><b>Education</b><br><br><em>Juris Doctor</em><span>&nbsp;from Seattle University School of Law;&nbsp;</span><em>Master of Physician Assistant Studies</em><span>&nbsp;and&nbsp;</span><em>Bachelor of Science</em><span>&nbsp;from the University of Nebraska Medical Center;&nbsp;</span><em>Associate of Science</em><span>&nbsp;from George Washington University.</span><br><br><b>Community Service</b><br><br><span>Founded a veteran-focused 501(c)(4); volunteer for Salmon for Soldiers.</span><br><br><b>Statement</b><br><br><span>I’m running to lower the cost of living, protect your constitutional rights, and stop out of control government spending. I will oppose new taxes, fight the unconstitutional income tax, and demand a responsible budget that funds public safety, education, and infrastructure. I will defend parents’ authority to raise and protect their children. I will defend your right to elect and keep a sheriff of the people and cut fees, regulations, and hidden costs that punish working families and small businesses. I will oppose any mega airport here and fight for accountable government.</span><br><br>",
